--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
Expression-form non-type template arguments (e.g., X % Y in
gcd<Y, X % Y>) are not resolved during template argument
processing in typecheck_expr. Simple identifier arguments
(e.g., Y as an ambiguous node) are resolved through the
template map, but compound expressions containing template
parameter references are not type-checked before being used
as template arguments.
Root cause of libc++ std::ratio and std::chrono::duration failures.
